document.write('<STYLE type=text/css>div#rsstojs A:link {COLOR: ;font-family:; font-size:;}div#rsstojs A:visited {COLOR: ;font-family:; font-size:;}div#rsstojs A:hover {COLOR: ;font-family:; font-size:;}div#rsstojs { COLOR:  ;font-family:; font-size:; } p#rsslink { COLOR:  ;font-family:Arial; font-size:11; }</STYLE><div id=rsstojs style=background-color:;width:px; height:44px; align=><p class=channel ><a href=http://allafrica.com/latest/ target=_self >AllAfrica News: Latest</a><br></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030293.html target=_self >Egypt: Gunfire Kills Cairo Protesters - Reports</a><br/>Five Egyptians were reported killed Thursday at Tahrir Square in Cairo,  the scene of Wednesday&#39;s battles between forces backing President Hosni  Mubarak and the protesters occupying the square in a bid to force him to  resign.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030025.html target=_self >Egypt: Cairo Residents Grapple With Food Shortages, Security Threats</a><br/>It is 6.00am and Rida Mansur feels she is running late. The 57-year-old mother of five has to get to the vegetable market early to buy food for her family before things run out. But she was not lucky today: All she could get were a few expensive tomatoes and cucumbers.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102020940.html target=_self >Zimbabwe: Cabinet Split Over Deputy PM Position</a><br/>Sharp differences have emerged in Zimbabwe&#39;s fragile unity government over the fate of one of the deputy Prime Ministers who was demoted by his party but has not left his post after receiving support from President Robert Mugabe.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030266.html target=_self >Côte d&#39;Ivoire: African Union Plans Month of Action on Crisis</a><br/>A High Level Panel has been set up by the African Union to send a team of experts to Côte d&#39;Ivoire and come up with a solution to the political impasse that would be binding on both incumbent Laurent Gbagbo and his rival for the presidency, Alassane Ouattara.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030173.html target=_self >Uganda: 70 MPs Must Lose Seats, Orders Court</a><br/>The Uganda Government was by last evening still studying a Court judgment in which all Independent MPs who were nominated as flag bearers while holding their posts were required to vacate their seats in Parliament.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030056.html target=_self >Nigeria: Sect Members Threaten More Violence</a><br/>Radical Islamist sect in the north, Boko Haram, yesterday threatened to embark on full blown war against the government, even as it claimed responsibility for the killing of a prominent local politician last week.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030026.html target=_self >Comoros: Missing Guns Delay Demobilization</a><br/>Hundreds of weapons used in a revolt on Anjouan, one of three islands in the Comoros archipelago, remain unaccounted for, causing the government to change its strategy for disarmament, demobilization and reintegration.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030024.html target=_self >Sudan: Govt Used Excessive Force Against Demonstrators, Says Rights Group</a><br/>Sudanese authorities used excessive force during largely peaceful protests that began on January 30, 2011, Human Rights Watch said today.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102020917.html target=_self >Egypt: Clashes Rock Cairo as Pro-Mubarak Forces Hit Back</a><br/>Dozens of people have been injured in clashes between supporters and opponents of Egyptian President Hosni Mubarak on Cairo&#39;s Tahrir Square Wednesday.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030322.html target=_self >Zimbabwe: Filtering Fact Fiction About D.I.Y. Water Treatment</a><br/>The southern Zimbabwean city of Bulawayo has not been spared the heavy rains that have fallen across Southern Africa; the water is welcome in this semi-arid part of the country, but the coming of the rainy season has provoked fresh memories of the 2008 cholera epidemic.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030267.html target=_self >South Africa: Registration Delays Keep HIV Drugs Off Shelves</a><br/>Delays in drug registration by the country&#39;s Medicines Control Council (MCC), contribute to depriving South African HIV patients of important fixed dose combination antiretroviral (ARV) drugs.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030214.html target=_self >Uganda: Diversify Coffee Exports, Expert Advises</a><br/>Uganda should diversify its coffee exports to hedge against uncertainties that may come out of market concentration, a senior trade official has said.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030213.html target=_self >Uganda: Court Ruling Guards Against Political Opportunism - Law Society</a><br/>The Uganda Law Society yesterday dismissed the possibility of a constitutional crisis arising out of a Constitutional Court declaration that all MPs who got nominated for this month&#39;s general election on a platform different from the party ticket on which they currently hold their parliamentary seats must vacate the House.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030141.html target=_self >Somalia: UN Official Urges Concerted Response to Humanitarian Crisis</a><br/>The top United Nations humanitarian official today called for a concerted response to the crisis in Somalia, where a worsening drought has led to severe shortages of water, food and pasture, and swelled the number of people in need of assistance to 2.4 million.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030140.html target=_self >Congo-Kinshasa: UN Peacekeepers Rescue Kidnapped Police</a><br/>United Nations peacekeepers in the eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) have rescued six national police officers kidnapped by rebels without paying a ransom or firing a shot, relying on diplomacy and their superior numbers.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030132.html target=_self >Kenya: Security Chiefs&#39; Bid to Suspend Ocampo Probe Fails</a><br/>A bid to suspend the ICC prosecutor Luis Moreno-Ocampo&#39;s investigations have failed, as Kenya moved its lobbying for a deferral on the Hague cases to the United Nations Security Council.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030058.html target=_self >Angola: Questions About China&#39;s &#39;Win-Win&#39; Relationship With Nation</a><br/>Crouched on their haunches on the edge of a crumbling pavement, a group of Chinese construction workers are eating noodles from tin bowls, wearing floppy straw hats under their green safety helmets to protect them from the aggressive midday sun.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030055.html target=_self >Egypt: Mubarak Supporters Attacked Journalists, Says Group</a><br/>Reporters Without Borders unreservedly condemns today&#39;s shocking attacks on BBC, Al Jazeera, CNN, Al-Arabiya and ABC News journalists by Mubarak supporters who were reportedly accompanied by plainclothes police.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030036.html target=_self >Nigeria: We Are Responsible for Borno Killings, Says Sect</a><br/>The Islamic Religious sect ,Boko Haram, has claimed responsibility for the killing last Friday in Maiduguri, the Borno state capital of seven people including the brother and cousin of the state governor, Senator Modu Sheriff.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030029.html target=_self >Mozambique: The Nation, Gays and UN Human Rights Bodies</a><br/>The Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights appears to believe that homosexuality is illegal in Mozambique.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030028.html target=_self >South Africa: Welfare Payments - a Panacea for Poverty?</a><br/>With nearly one in three South Africans expected to receive state assistance in the form of welfare benefits during the 2011/12 financial year, commentators are wondering how the country can afford to keep providing an ever expanding social safety net.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030027.html target=_self >Egypt: U.S. Says Violence in Must Stop, Transition Must Begin</a><br/>The White House strongly condemns outrageous and deplorable violence that has broken out in Cairo and other Egyptian cities and has renewed its call for political change to begin in the country.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102020778.html target=_self >Namibia: Nation Takes Another Step to Gas Production</a><br/>PARTNERS in the Kudu gas field have taken another baby step in developing the project which will pump 500 megawatts of power into the Namibian grid and allow the country to export another 300 megawatts.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102020689.html target=_self >Egypt: A Million Voices, One Message</a><br/>Organisers called it Egypt&#39;s million man march. Whether they achieved that targeted head count is unclear, but their message was unequivocal.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102020630.html target=_self >Kenya: Central Bank Lowers Policy Rate to Spur Lending</a><br/>The Central Bank of Kenya is looking to speed up growth to help the economy offset the impact of the global commodity boom on local prices.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030421.html target=_self >Nigeria: Electoral Commission to Release List of Candidates February 6</a><br/>The Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) is to release the official list of candidates submitted by political parties to contest the 2011 general elections by February 6.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030417.html target=_self >Nigeria: ADB Trains Nomadic Education Field Officers on Entrepreneurship</a><br/>The African Development Bank (ADB) under the African Development Fund Assisted Skills Training and Vocational Education Project (ADB-STVEP) is training field officers of the National Commission for Nomadic Education (NCNE) on entrepreneurship.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030414.html target=_self >Nigeria: Jonathan - I Have Nothing to Lose By Contesting</a><br/>President Goodluck Jonathan said yesterday that he decided to contest, in spite of advice by some people not to, in order to exercise his constitutional right and not to give room for any excuse.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030413.html target=_self >Nigeria: Reps Want Specialist Hospital for President</a><br/>The House of Representatives&#39; Committee on Defence has criticized the top echelon of the Defence Headquarters for abandoning the building of a specialist hospital in Abuja to cater for the health needs of the president and top military officers in the country.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://allafrica.com/stories/201102030361.html target=_self >Nigeria: Country Increasingly Vulnerable to Cancer</a><br/>Cancer is one of the world&#39;s most killer diseases today that has defied total cure. It is one of the major causes of death in Nigeria especially among the women who die from cervical and breast cancer.</p></div> <p id=rsslink >Powered by: <a title=RSS-to-JavaScript.com: Free RSS to JavaScript Converter href=http://www.rss-to-javascript.com target=_powered alt=Free Content for Virtually Any Web-site! RSS-to-Javascript.com> RSS-to-JavaScript.com</a></font></p>');